  "headline": "MPR Sets Four Day Grace Period For Vice President Candidates Data",
  "seoTitle": "Mabes Polri and MPR Verify Vice President Candidates",
  "metaDescription": "The MPR verification team has granted vice president candidates four days to address document discrepancies following consultations with Mabes Polri.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The MPR verification team is granting candidates a four-day window to fulfill any outstanding administrative requirements.",
    "Verification involves cross-referencing candidate documentation with institutions including the Supreme Court, the KPK, the Ministry of Finance, and Mabes Polri.",
    "Discussions are ongoing within the MPR regarding whether the selection of the replacement vice president will be decided via consensus or voting."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The People's Consultative Assembly of the Republic of Indonesia (MPR) is currently overseeing the verification process for vice presidential candidates following a vacancy in the office of the vice president. The Ad Hoc Committee has confirmed that candidates are subject to rigorous checks, including health assessments and document validation. To ensure transparency, the verification team has reached out to various government bodies, including the Ministry of Home Affairs, which confirmed the validity of population documents, and institutions like Mabes Polri, the Supreme Court, and the KPK for institutional vetting. Candidates have been given a four-day extension to rectify any administrative shortcomings identified during this review. Meanwhile, political factions within the MPR are debating the formal selection mechanism, with proposals currently split between reaching a consensus through deliberation or proceeding with a plenary session vote, which is tentatively scheduled for early December 2026.",
